 more carefully - the chart on page 21 would be FO-1 (Gross obligations by object class) - which is on page 18 per the table of contents, but the chart showing the visual representation might be on page 21. \n\nI confirm the totals match perfectly. The FO-1 table shows $614,968 million as the gross obligations outside the Federal Government, which aligns precisely with the figure I used in my calculation. This corroboration strengthens my confidence in the analysis.\n\nI'll round the percentage to the nearest whole number, which comes out to 69%.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_464973a44a00e662","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me double-check the table structure from the JSON\nimport json\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1988_09.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Find the FO-1 table - it's a table that shows Outside = 614,968\nelements = data.get('document', {}).get('elements', [])\nfor e in elements:\n    if e.get('type') == 'table':\n        content = e.get('content', '')\n        if 'Gross obligations incurred' in content and 'Outside' in content:\n            # Print just enough to confirm\n            print('Found FO-1 table')\n            print('Content snippet:', content[500:1500])\n            break\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
